{"abstract":"This paper presents key characteristics of Web3 and how the traditional business model canvas (BMC) requires update to support managers in the Web3 industry. The characteristics of Web3 include Dapps, wallets, interoperability, tokenization, distributed ownership, decentralized communities, creator economy, and token economy. This study investigates how a business model in Web3 is different from the traditional BMC by Osterwalder and Pigneur (2010) based on a Delphi study with a panel of eight experts from the Web3 industry. The contribution of the research outlines a nascent Web3 business model canvas with seven building blocks, which are complemented by two overarching components specific to the nascent Web3 business models: value co-creation and value distribution. Furthermore, the model expands on the blocks of community and customer, tokenomics, and incentive and reward structures.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kaae, Christina","Pedersen, Asger Balle","Agerskov, Signe","Beck, Roman"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712564"],"event":{"acronym":"HICSS","title":"Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blockchain","Business model canvas","Tokens","Web3","decentralized business models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"web000000000003 decentralized business models","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101770436/paper_eca8e1cf-08db-452d-8ac2-630a0e5ff171_final_4_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712564","identifier":[{"id":"85194181803","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f13bfdad-47c2-4462-b8c8-75d4674c0e1a"],"keyword":["blockchain","business model canvas","decentralized business models","tokens","web3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-145DAF341E6B8D62269F9C1E4D54469F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101770436/paper_eca8e1cf-08db-452d-8ac2-630a0e5ff171_final_4_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"kaaepau","last":"Kaae","name":"Kaae, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Balle","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"09ec1bda-4550-4a83-8480-fe742d77e882","name":"Pedersen, Asger Balle","orcid":"0000-0002-3390-2831","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe","key":"agerskovpau","last":"Agerskov","locid":"bb557cdc-29c2-4445-9b5f-fea28ba8d6a9","name":"Agerskov, Signe","orcid":"0000-0002-6382-0300","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roman","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","locid":"d72cc0d6-fe4f-4392-bf88-243e5d7e36e5","name":"Beck, Roman","orcid":"0000-0002-6341-2382","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["10603425","15301605"],"issn_org":["10603425"],"journal":"Proceedings of the Annual Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Annual Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"rev