{"abstract":"Enterprise architects and IT systems developers must often decide ad hoc how to identify, assess and mitigate ethical issues of autonomous, rule-based systems based on blockchain technology. As blockchain systems are decentralized and immutable, developers must assess ethical risks, not only on an individual level but also on a network level along the life-cycle stages of a blockchain system. These ethical issues should be addressed and ideally mitigated by clearly defined norms and values that are intentionally incorporated in a blockchain system. As a reference for a normative system, we have chosen the European Union and its ethical values to discuss them in the context of ethical issues emerging from blockchain systems. This paper presents a top-down approach that establishes ethical guidelines for blockchain systems based on ethical issues mapped against European values.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Agerskov, Signe","Pedersen, Asger Balle","Beck, Roman"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677307"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blockchain","Ethics","Guidelines","Information systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ethical guidelines for blockchain systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/97076034/ecis23a_sub1334_cam_i7_6_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677307","ids":["itu-47051b93-43ae-48be-9612-eb011ab63493"],"keyword":["blockchain","ethics","guidelines","information systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-89C6FD3ED8BA77B536F4C993E8BEAD23"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aisel.aisnet.org/ecis2023_rp/275","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/97076034/ecis23a_sub1334_cam_i7_6_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://plu.mx/plum/a/?bepress_url_id=https%3A%2F%2Faisel.aisnet.org%2Fecis2023_rp%2F275","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe","key":"agerskovpau","last":"Agerskov","locid":"bb557cdc-29c2-4445-9b5f-fea28ba8d6a9","name":"Agerskov, Signe","orcid":"0000-0002-6382-0300","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Balle","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"09ec1bda-4550-4a83-8480-fe742d77e882","name":"Pedersen, Asger Balle","orcid":"0000-0002-3390-2831","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roman","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","locid":"d72cc0d6-fe4f-4392-bf88-243e5d7e36e5","name":"Beck, Roman","orcid":"0000-0002-6341-2382","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00000034"],"journal":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","status":"p","title":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","title_org":"European Conference of Information Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-47051b93-43ae-48be-9612-eb011ab63493"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ethical Guidelines for Blockchain Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677307","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Cryptographic tokens are one of the cornerstones of the new blockchain world but the knowledge about these digital objects is still limited. In this research, we argue that crypto tokens, cryptographically secured digital tokens connected to DLT systems, form socio-technical systems through their reciprocal relationship with their foundational DLT systems. We also argue that today’s crypto token systems evolved out of earlier physical and digital token systems, a socio-technical transition facilitated by changes in the wider socio-cultural, economic, and technical environment. Based on an extensive structured literature review as well as the application of text analytics methods to more than 506 blockchain whitepapers, we develop two results: a crypto token classification built around three crypto token archetypes, and a crypto token system taxonomy. Our findings are relevant for both blockchain researchers and practitioners alike by enhancing our understanding of complex blockchain systems.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Schwiderowski, Jan","Pedersen, Asger Balle","Beck, Roman"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384932"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blockchain","Taxonomy","Token","token system"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"crypto tokens and token systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/95285808/Crypto_Tokens_and_Token_Systems_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384932","identifier":[{"id":"85150186196","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f8ce9682-53c8-46c3-84df-27092ec427bc"],"keyword":["Blockchain","taxonomy","token","token system"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-25E7498C830C1E6AE8D5603E9F74A670"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/95285808/Crypto_Tokens_and_Token_Systems_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"schwiderowskipau","last":"Schwiderowski","name":"Schwiderowski, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Balle","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"09ec1bda-4550-4a83-8480-fe742d77e882","name":"Pedersen, Asger Balle","orcid":"0000-0002-3390-2831","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roman","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","locid":"d72cc0d6-fe4f-4392-bf88-243e5d7e36e5","name":"Beck, Roman","orcid":"0000-0002-6341-2382","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10796-023-10382-w","issn":["13873326","15729419"],"issn_org":["13873326"],"journal":"Information Systems Frontiers","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Information Systems Frontiers"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85150186196"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f8ce9682-53c8-46c3-84df-27092ec427bc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Crypto Tokens and Token Systems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384932","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Information technology (IT) has radically changed the financial services industry, with the most recent transformation toward Fintech and decentralized finance (DeFi), driven by blockchain. Especially non-fungible token (NFT) assets within DeFi are redefining how value is created and disseminated, for instance in the art industry. However, DeFi and NFT market dynamics are not yet well understood. Using a thematic analysis based on 14 interviews with major NFT stakeholders (i.e., marketplace providers, artists, and investing collectors), we identify these NFT stakeholders’ different motivations and strategic options and explain the value creation and capture dynamics in the NFT art market resulting from their interactions. We argue for decomposing an NFT’s value into an NFT-intrinsic and an NFT-extrinsic part. Finally, we elaborate that art NFTs are not a new class of assets because many of their properties are similar to related assets such as physical art and cryptocurrencies.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Schwiderowski, Jan","Pedersen, Asger Balle","Jensen, Jonas Kasper","Beck, Roman"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689195"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blockchain","Decentralized Finance DeFi","Digital Assets","Financial markets","Value creation","non fungible tokens NFT"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"value creation and capture in decentralized finance markets non fungible tokens as a class of digital assets","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12525-023-00658-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-689195","identifier":[{"id":"85169135145","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b69f3082-70be-4f9e-b2a8-83e650d09239"],"keyword":["blockchain","decentralized finance (Defi)","digital assets","financial markets","non-fungible tokens (NFT)","value creation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E857A6EEAFC0733210A1A42B5391B5A0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s12525-023-00658-z.pdf?pdf=button","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108495119/s12525-023-00658-z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s12525-023-00658-z","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"schwiderowskipau","last":"Schwiderowski","name":"Schwiderowski, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Balle","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"09ec1bda-4550-4a83-8480-fe742d77e882","name":"Pedersen, Asger Balle","orcid":"0000-0002-3390-2831","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Kasper","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jonas Kasper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roman","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","locid":"d72cc0d6-fe4f-4392-bf88-243e5d7e36e5","name":"Beck, Roman","orcid":"0000-0002-6341-2382","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12525-023-00658-z","issn":["10196781","14228890"],"issn_org":["10196781"],"journal":"Electronic Markets","paperid":"45","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Electronic Markets","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85169135145"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b69f3082-70be-4f9e-b2a8-83e650d09239"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Value Creation and Capture in Decentralized Finance Markets: Non-Fungible Tokens as a Class of Digital Assets","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-689195","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Blockchain research tends to focus on technical improvements and their potential for efficiency and productivity, repeatedly at the cost of comprehending the complex reciprocal interaction between social and technical aspects. One of the technical challenges for blockchain systems is scalability. Interoperability has proven effective in addressing scalability by offloading transactions via bridges, enhancing flexibility and portability for, e.g., tokens. As a result, we investigate how interoperability is organized in blockchain systems and what implications it might bring. In this research, we develop an on-ledger analytics prototype, which facilitates the examinations of NFT bridges and theorizes about the dimensions of interoperability. Practical implications reveal that hiding a token’s track in an otherwise supposedly transparent system is possible. We provide evidence that current research may only consider a subset of a token’s history among blockchain systems. Ultimately, we claim that interoperability among blockchain systems can lead to decreased transparency.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Iversen, Hampus MIchael Wadum","Schmidt, Tobias Ærboe","Pedersen, Asger Balle","Beck, Roman"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-701227"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blockchain","Information Systems IS Research","Information systems","Interoperability","Tokens","Transparency"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to cross the bridge interoperability among blockchain systems interoperability among blockchain systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101770173/icis23a-sub1171-cam-i9_13_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-701227","ids":["itu-14631e3b-8d1c-42e2-aa15-1fed22e7b14d"],"keyword":["Information Systems (IS) Research","blockchain","information systems","interoperability","tokens","transparency"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-46E9D755E2152288894AF6E60DEF2623"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101770173/icis23a-sub1171-cam-i9_13_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hampus MIchael Wadum","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","name":"Iversen, Hampus MIchael Wadum","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias Ærboe","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Tobias Ærboe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Balle","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"09ec1bda-4550-4a83-8480-fe742d77e882","name":"Pedersen, Asger Balle","orcid":"0000-0002-3390-2831","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roman","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","locid":"d72cc0d6-fe4f-4392-bf88-243e5d7e36e5","name":"Beck, Roman","orcid":"0000-0002-6341-2382","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00000033"],"journal":"Proceedings / International Conference on Information Systems","status":"p","title":"Proceedings / International Conference on Information Systems","title_org":"Proceedings / International Conference on Information Systems (ICIS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-14631e3b-8d1c-42e2-aa15-1fed22e7b14d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How to cross the bridge: Interoperability among blockchain systems : Interoperability among blockchain systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-701227","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"A wide range of socioeconomic hopes are pinned on the transformative power of blockchain technologies. However, blockchain databases have noticeable drawbacks (i.e., scalability, capacity, latency, privacy) that clearly indicate that blockchain is not a silver bullet for all problems. The application and selection of blockchain need to be carefully assessed, depending on the problem and use case at hand. To support IT decision-makers, we develop a ten-step decision path that can help determine whether or not the application of blockchain is justified and, if so, which kind of blockchain to use. We apply this decision path to the case of the maritime shipping industry, and develop a blockchain prototype for this case.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pedersen, Asger Balle","Risius, Marten","Beck, Roman"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382965"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Clemson University"],"keyword":["Blockchain","Decision Path","Decision making","Smart Contract Prototype","Supply chain management","Use Case Identification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"blockchain decision path when to use blockchains which blockchains do you mean","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17705/2msqe.00010","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382965","identifier":[{"id":"85067031201","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-72db87e3-36dd-4c59-ba00-ca3a057a3a30"],"keyword":["Blockchain","Decision Path","Decision-Making","Smart Contract Prototype","Supply Chain Management","Use-Case Identification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-779B15552F6B193E33A1BE32CAF65206"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17705/2msqe.00010","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83594249/MISQe_BC_in_the_Maritime_Shipping_Industry_Revision.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"clemson university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Clemson University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Balle","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"09ec1bda-4550-4a83-8480-fe742d77e882","name":"Pedersen, Asger Balle","orcid":"0000-0002-3390-2831","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marten","key":"risiuspau","last":"Risius","name":"Risius, Marten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roman","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","locid":"d72cc0d6-fe4f-4392-bf88-243e5d7e36e5","name":"Beck, Roman","orcid":"0000-0002-6341-2382","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.17705/2msqe.00010","issn":["15401960","15401979"],"issn_org":["15401960"],"issue":"2","journal":"MIS Quarterly Executive","paperid":"3","publisher":"Indiana University Press","status":"p","title":"MIS Quarterly Executive","title_org":"M I S Quarterly Executive","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85067031201"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-72db87e3-36dd-4c59-ba00-ca3a057a3a30"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Blockchain Decision Path: When to Use Blockchains? Which blockchains do you mean?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382965","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
